# D3 done — Environment blueprint + snapshot (merge gate fixed, commit ac0cf67)

## What happened
The gate failure was a **corrupt git index** in this worktree: the index file at
`.git/worktrees/devin-d3/index` was completely zeroed (589,020 bytes of 0x00),
so every git command failed with `error: bad signature 0x00000000 / fatal:
index file corrupt`. A partially-applied merge had also left 48 working-tree
files fully zeroed on disk.

## Root-cause fix (no tests weakened)
1. Moved the zeroed index aside (`index.corrupt.bak`) and ran `git reset` to
   rebuild the index from HEAD. All D3 work was already committed, so nothing
   was lost.
2. Verified every untracked file was manus-parity content (no D3-unique work on
   disk) and removed the corrupted leftovers with `git clean -fd`.
3. Ran a clean `git merge manus-parity`. Conflicts in `package.json`,
   `src/server/http.ts`, `src/server/runTools.ts` were resolved **keeping both
   sides** (D3 env routes/tools + manus-parity wiki/playbooks/test-isolation).
4. Committed the merge as `ac0cf67`.

## D3 feature (unchanged, verified still present)
- `src/tools/envSnapshot.ts` — `loam.env.yaml` blueprint + cached snapshot
  builder under `data/env-snapshots/<project>/<hash>`, `bootTaskFromSnapshot`,
  secret redaction, hash-based reuse.
- Tools `env_blueprint_generate`, `env_build_status` (registered in the tool
  registry and in `ALWAYS_ON_TOOLS`).
- `src/server/routes/envBuilds.ts` + route wiring in `src/server/http.ts`.
- `src/scripts/check-env-builds.ts`.

## Independent re-validation (2026-10-23, second pass)

Every claim above was re-checked from scratch rather than trusted:

- **Union audit (set-based, line level).** Extracted the pre-merge base `088b4f2`,
  D3 parent `053cd0e`, parity tip `03f8aef` and merge `ac0cf67` for all three
  conflicted files, then compared line multisets. Result: `d3LinesMissing=0` and
  `parityLinesMissing=0` for `package.json`, `src/server/http.ts` and
  `src/server/runTools.ts`. Nothing from either side was dropped. Line counts are
  exactly additive (merge = base + D3's additions + parity's additions).
- **No test weakening.** `git diff 03f8aef HEAD -- '*__tests__*'` is purely
  additive: 658 insertions, 0 deletions; `runTools.test.ts` only gained the D3
  union lines. `git diff --diff-filter=D` against parity is empty (no test file
  deleted). 4 new D3 test files added.
- **Gates re-run with exit codes captured:** `npx tsc --noEmit` exit 0;
  `npm run build:server` exit 0 (dist/server.cjs 20,272,471 bytes);
  `next build` exit 0 (compiled successfully, 25/25 static pages);
  D3 env tests 24/24; tools 632/632; server 414/414; agent+llm+memory 305/305;
  web vitest 437/437 (66 files).
- **Conflict markers:** `git grep -E '^(<<<<<<<|>>>>>>>)$' HEAD` returns nothing.
- **Forbidden paths:** `git diff --name-only 03f8aef HEAD -- docs/handoff/watchdog.ps1
  qa/ packages/tests/visual/baselines` returns nothing (count 0).
- **Tree state:** `git status --porcelain` empty (0 entries); `git merge-tree
  --write-tree manus-parity HEAD` exits 0 (no re-emerging conflict);
  `git rev-list --count HEAD..manus-parity` = 0 (not behind).
- **Merge shape:** `ac0cf67` has two parents, `053cd0e` (D3) and `03f8aef` (parity
  tip); `manus-parity` is an ancestor of HEAD.
- **Encoding:** `.jdone` is UTF-8 without BOM and contains no U+FFFD; Arabic
  text is intact in `src/agent/masterPromptText.ts` (388 Arabic chars) and
  `packages/web/src/i18n/ar.json` (11,266).

### Note on `git fsck`
`git fsck` in this shared repo prints `error: bad signature 0x00000000 / fatal:
index file corrupt`. This is **not** caused by this worktree. `fsck` walks every
registered worktree, and `devin-d19` and `devin-d4` have fully zeroed indexes
(signature `0x00000000`). Every other worktree (including this one and the
`manus-parity` main worktree) has a valid `DIRC` index, and the error reproduces
identically from an unrelated worktree. Confirmed the object store itself is
sound: `git verify-pack -v .../pack-4f9df149...idx` reports `ok`, a fresh
`git clone` of the same repo runs `git fsck` at exit 0, and a bare clone also
exits 0. This worktree's index is valid (593,276 bytes, signature `DIRC`,
version 2) and every index-reading command (`ls-files`, `status`, `diff`) works.

## Gates (all pass, run from the worktree root)
1. `npx tsc --noEmit` — PASS
2. `npm run build:server` — PASS (dist/server.cjs 19.3mb)
3. `(cd packages/web && npx next build)` — PASS (Next.js 16.4.2, 25 static pages)
4. Tests:
   - `node --import tsx --test src/tools/__tests__/envSnapshot.test.ts src/tools/__tests__/envSnapshotE2E.test.ts src/server/__tests__/envBuildRoutes.test.ts src/server/__tests__/taskWorkspace.test.ts` — 24/24 PASS
   - `node --import tsx --test src/tools/__tests__/*.test.ts` — 632/632 PASS
   - `node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/*.test.ts` — 414/414 PASS
   - `node --import tsx --test src/agent/__tests__/*.test.ts src/llm/__tests__/*.test.ts src/memory/__tests__/*.test.ts` — 305/305 PASS
   - `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run)` — 437/437 PASS (66 files)

## Acceptance criteria coverage
- blueprint generated from a fixture repo: `envSnapshot.test.ts` ("generates a
  blueprint from the manifest and writes loam.env.yaml")
- first build runs setup steps, second boot reuses snapshot (counter assert):
  "runs the setup steps once, then reuses the cached snapshot" + E2E real-shell
  test
- hash change triggers rebuild: "the hash changes when the lockfile changes" /
  "rebuilds when the hash changes" / "bootTaskFromSnapshot ignores a stale
  snapshot after the lockfile changes"
- secret values never appear in logs: "preserves hand-written secrets as NAMES
  only", "injects a resolved secret into the child env only", "redacts a secret
  echoed by a setup step", "fails the build when a referenced secret is missing"

