# N1 - Run-graph model: done (merge gate fixed, commit ac0aed3)

The `.jgatefail.txt` failure was `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity`.
Ran `git merge manus-parity` (tip `0c97967`); one file conflicted:
- `src/config.ts`: kept BOTH sides — the N1 `runGraph?: { enabled: boolean }`
  config field (HEAD) and parity's `coding?: { enabled, chain, logEdits }` field
  (C17 coding-model routing). Both are present in the `Config` interface and in
  `DEFAULTS` (`runGraph: { enabled: true }`, `coding: { enabled: true, chain: [], logEdits: true }`).

A typecheck failure that the merge exposed was fixed (not worked around):
`src/graph/runGraph.ts` has an exhaustive `switch (event.type)` over the
`AgentEvent` union. manus-parity added two new event kinds (`cache_usage` from
J10, `video_studio_command` from fc-03), so the `default` arm's
`const _exhaustive: never = event` no longer type-checked. Both new kinds are
live-only signals with no canvas node of their own, so they were added to the
existing no-op case list alongside `todo`/`phase`/`task-status`/etc. No test was
weakened or deleted; the graph's golden replay, status-transition and 10k-node
performance tests are unchanged.

Resolution committed as `ac0aed3 merge manus-parity into neo-n1: resolve
config.ts, extend runGraph event switch`. `git merge-tree --write-tree
manus-parity HEAD` exits 0, so no conflict re-emerges.

## Gates (all run from the worktree root, on merged tip ac0aed3)
- `npx tsc --noEmit`                          -> exit 0
- `npm run build:server`                      -> exit 0 (dist/server.cjs 19.2mb, pdf worker copied)
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)`       -> exit 0 (Next.js 16.4.2, 25/25 static pages)
- `node --import tsx --test src/graph/__tests__/*.test.ts`
  -> tests 11, pass 11, fail 0
  (replay builds the golden tree; JSON export round-trip; layout/depth/stats;
  illegal transitions rejected; restart resume; forward-only status rules;
  10k nodes load; deterministic ids; malformed-export rejection)
- `node --import tsx --test src/agent/__tests__/loopHooks.test.ts src/protocol/__tests__/cacheUsageEvents.test.ts src/agent/__tests__/cacheUsageAccounting.test.ts`
  -> tests 19, pass 19, fail 0

Working tree clean; no existing test weakened; no forbidden path touched.

## What N1 delivers
- `src/graph/store.ts`: the `run_node` JSON store (id, run_id, parent_ids[],
  type, status, data, position, version, created, updated) with
  `RUN_NODE_TYPES`, `RUN_NODE_STATUSES`, deterministic `eventNodeId` hashing,
  and `RunGraphExport`/`importRun`/`exportRun` (share/replay import).
- `src/graph/status.ts`: the status transition table (`assertTransition`,
  `canTransition`) and the exported status vocabulary.
- `src/graph/runGraph.ts`: `RunGraph` — replays a recorded event log into the
  tree, adapts existing agent events (plan, plan_step, critique, verify,
  tool_call, tool_result, artifact_published, ...) into nodes, keeps a live
  cursor, resumes after restart, and produces a layered layout plus aggregate
  stats. One journal transaction per event (one per replay), which is what keeps
  a 10k-node replay under the 300 ms budget.

